      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "PowerShell solution (co-authored by Microsoft Copilot):\n\n```\n\n$path = \"$env:USERPROFILE\\AppData\\LocalLow\\VRChat\\VRChat\\LocalPlayerModerations\"\n\n$patternA = '^[0-9a-z]{10}-show-hide-user\\.vrcset$'\n\n$patternB = '^usr_[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}-show-hide-user\\.vrcset$'\n\n$files = Get-ChildItem -Path $path -File | Where-Object {\n\n    $_.Name -match $patternA -or $_.Name -match $patternB\n\n}\n\nforeach ($file in $files) {\n\n    $content = Get-Content $file.FullName\n\n    $newContent = $content | Where-Object { $_ -notmatch ' 005$' }\n\n    Set-Content -Path $file.FullName -Value $newContent\n\n}\n\n```\n\nClose any running instances of the VRChat client, run the PowerShell script, and start the VRChat client again. \"Show avatar\" moderations will be reset to the default state (= Safety Shield) targeting every VRChat user shown, and these changes will be applied to every VRChat account used to login from the current Windows user profile.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
